## The default screen window for a non-square Format is +-frameAspectRatio
## in x, not the canonical +-1 NDC cube: GMANPolygonClipper::clip must
## clip perspective geometry against that window, the same bound
## GMANViewingSystem::screenToRaster maps to the raster. Format 800x200
## (aspect 4, no RiScreenWindow) puts that window at [-4,4]x[-1,1]; one
## flat, camera-facing rectangle spans world x=[-19.5,19.5] at z=5, so
## camera-space x/z reaches ndc.x=+-3.9 -- inside the true window, hard
## outside the old fixed +-1 cube. A render still clipping at +-1 shows
## only a narrow centre band; the fix fills within 10px of both edges.
Display "wideframe.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 800 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [90]
# Explicit, not the RI_EPSILON-near default: SPEC.md Section 8's near-clip
# precision defect corrupts geometry flat or narrow in z hardest, and this
# rectangle's four vertices share one z.
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.3]
Sides 2
Color [0.8 0.4 0.2]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1.0]
Polygon "P" [-19.5 -2 0  19.5 -2 0  19.5 2 0  -19.5 2 0]
WorldEnd
